# CTO6092: eligibility field closure and two-site constructor proposal

The next owning readers close the previous box165 boundary: it is the old bonding-curve is_holder_reward boolean, default false before payload117. The original6092 wallet eligibility is suppressed for an existing holder-reward creator and for a shared-config creator, then requires a nonzero old creator, System owner, nonexecutable account and nonwritable flag. There is no independent cashback exclusion at this eligibility gate; fee-Some/cashback can already fail earlier. Current wallet omits the explicit old-holder/shared eligibility terms. This is a bounded branch/formula result, not complete CTO or later payout/CPI/event equivalence.

A separate unapplied constructor-only patch replaces BOTH current numeric6092 expressions with the existing named owning Anchor constructor. This is supported independently of the predicate domain: where the existing source branch returns6092, it changes only error representation to the proved name/message/code/owned family with empty compared fields. It preserves every predicate, guard order, line count and other operation. Its natural source origins115/123 still differ from original556/file38; it does not reproduce the complete original error object byte-for-byte. The second current site remains dominated/redundant under immutable flags. No source, build, status or selected artifact is changed.

