## Current source difference and precise remaining limits

Current wallet=old!=default && owner==System && !executable lacks the old-is_holder_reward gate. Its existing shared variable has the same key/owner/nonempty Boolean when data length can be read. The explicit !shared term is absent from wallet; ordinary same-key AccountInfo aliasing may already force a shared creator's owner to FEES and suppress current wallet, but this packet does not replace the original explicit term with that transitive runtime assumption.

Current shared evaluates owner, then data-empty, then key equality. Original shared evaluates key, then owner, then data-empty. That short-circuit/borrow or panic precedence difference is a separate concrete remaining edge: Boolean agreement on accessible data does not prove all data-borrow failures or AccountInfo alias states. No new borrow-failure probe is run. Likewise, the wallet local is reused for amount/sweep/frozen/payout/CPI/event choices; mapping this one eligibility check does not prove every later reuse and cleanup. No automatic wallet-local predicate patch is supplied on the strength of a before-frozen branch alone. The exact Boolean proposal is retained in witness.json for a further complete effect-order review.

## Constructor-only BOTH-sites correction

constructor-only-both-sites.patch is the complete proposed diff: return Err(err(6092)) becomes return Err(error!(PumpError::CtoCreatorAccountNotWritable)) at both existing sites, with no predicate or line changes. The unchanged original enum92/name28/message75/owned160-byte converter/empty compared-values/Source556 witness comes from the immutable prior packet and is retained through the same complete bodies here. The locked anchor-attribute-error0.31.2 archive is checked against the actual Pump lock and its factory member matches: error! uses Source(file!,line!), enum.name/into/to_string and compared_values=None, then From<AnchorError>. This corrects owning family and named fields; natural source metadata remains different and whole-error ABI/raw identity is not claimed.

The earlier wallet&&!writable return dominates the later wallet&&!wallet_frozen&&!writable expression using the same immutable local/flag. The second patch expression therefore has no independently demonstrated callable target site; changing both is a uniform constructor correction, not an invention of two target constructors or historical origins. The numeric err helper stays because other numeric sites remain.

Before any future selection, separately review actual emitted constructors/guard order/functions/callees/data with exact source37/tool/dependency/profile identities and backend diagnostics. Callable claims need a genuinely admitted, ordinarily signed target6092 fixture plus unchanged existing CTO error/success/CPI/state/event cases. Existing saved cases are historical. There is no new build, fixture, signature transaction, runtime/VM, networking, selected source/status/artifact or excluded-lane semantic change here.

verify.py uses only the Python standard library to rehash all exact source inputs, complete original function bounds/raw bodies/decoded records, all nine field stores/cursor helpers, actual shared/holder routes, FEES constant, old control witnesses, locked macro source and the exact unapplied two-expression diff. It verifies a recorded baseline; it is not a future candidate/current-selection gate.
